# Zod v4 Syntax Requirements

This project uses **Zod version 4**. All schema definitions must use Zod v4 syntax.

## Key Syntax Rules

### Email Validation

**Always use `z.email()` for email validation** - this is the Zod v4 preferred syntax:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Zod v4 preferred syntax (top-level)
const schema = z.object({
  email: z.email(),
});

// ❌ BAD - z.string().email() is deprecated in v4
const schema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
});
```

### String Format Validators

In Zod v4, string format validators are **top-level functions**, not methods on `z.string()`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Zod v4 syntax (top-level functions)
z.email()
z.uuid()
z.url()
z.httpUrl()
z.hostname()
z.emoji()
z.base64()
z.base64url()
z.hex()
z.jwt()
z.nanoid()
z.cuid()
z.cuid2()
z.ulid()
z.ipv4()
z.ipv6()
z.mac()
z.cidrv4()
z.cidrv6()
z.hash("sha256")
z.iso.date()
z.iso.time()
z.iso.datetime()
z.iso.duration()

// ❌ BAD - Method forms are deprecated in v4
z.string().email()
z.string().url()
z.string().uuid()
```

### String Methods

For string operations (not format validators), chain from `z.string()`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - String operations
z.string().min(1)
z.string().max(255)
z.string().length(5)
z.string().regex(/^[a-z]+$/)
z.string().startsWith("aaa")
z.string().endsWith("zzz")
z.string().includes("---")
z.string().trim()
z.string().toLowerCase()
z.string().toUpperCase()
z.string().nullable()
z.string().optional()
```

### Nullable and Optional

Use `.nullable()`, `.optional()`, or `.nullish()` as appropriate:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
z.string().nullable()      // string | null
z.string().optional()      // string | undefined
z.string().nullish()       // string | null | undefined
z.string().email().optional()  // Chaining works
```

### UUID Validation

Use `z.uuid()` - the top-level function is preferred:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Zod v4 preferred syntax
z.uuid()

// ❌ BAD - Method form is deprecated
z.string().uuid()
```

For more permissive UUID-like identifiers, use `z.guid()`:

```typescript
z.guid()  // Any 8-4-4-4-12 hex pattern (more permissive)
```

### Type Inference

Always use `z.infer<typeof schema>` for type extraction:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const schema = z.object({
  email: z.email(),
  name: z.string(),
});
type SchemaType = z.infer<typeof schema>;
```

## Validation Patterns

Always use `.safeParse()` for validation to handle errors gracefully:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const parsed = schema.safeParse(data);
if (!parsed.success) {
  return handleError(parsed.error);
}
const validData = parsed.data;
```
